  "interpretation": "An unmodified upstream OMP client now keeps durable sessions on both lanes: on the published RTX 5090 image and the installed RTX 4090 package, stock OMP 18.3.0 with only the documented fragments recalled its session across graceful restarts, including a new OMP process whose first request named no previous response and was restored from the session's checkpoint. New sessions start from the shared prefix: on the published image no measured fresh agent session fell back to a full prefill. The RTX 5090 durability workload, publication barrier and probe set match v0.7.4's results, and the RTX 4090 package passed its 15 canonical phases with the OMP 18.3.0 tool call. A managed RTX 4090 start can still fail intermittently while Windows holds most memory as standby cache (alphastorm/omp-ninfer#48). Automatic checkpoints stay best effort and universal warm reuse is not claimed.",
  "remaining_release_gates": [
    "external-installation acceptance against the published v0.6.9-qwen38-5090-beta.1 component and runtime image",
    "fresh upstream OMP platform and documented-route acceptance"
